The address parsing rules are a reimplementation of the `parse-address` package
by Hassansin (https://github.com/hassansin/parse-address), distributed under the
ISC licence. That package descends from the Perl `Geo::StreetAddress::US` module
and from the United States Postal Service publication 28 street-type table. The
rules themselves encode the published standard; this crate is an independent
reimplementation for Rust and shares no code with it. The pattern text and the
lookup tables were extracted mechanically from the reference by
`scripts/fuzz/address-parser/extract_patterns.js`, and every case in
`tests/fixtures/oracle.tsv` was labelled by the reference itself.

